 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# Content not properly moved when merging table cells\n\n## Current problem\n\nWhen merging table cells, the content from one cell is not properly moved to the target cell. This happens specifically when working with structured document tags (SDT) and other complex content.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a document with a table\n2. Add complex content to a cell (like structured document tags or nested tables)\n3. Try to merge this cell with another cell\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\n# Create a document with a table\ndoc = Document()\ntable = doc.add_table(rows=2, cols=2)\n\n# Add some content to the first cell\ncell1 = table.cell(0, 0)\ncell1.add_paragraph(\"Content in cell 1\")\n\n# Add a nested table to the second cell\ncell2 = table.cell(0, 1)\nnested_table = cell2.add_table(rows=1, cols=1)\nnested_table.cell(0, 0).text = \"Nested table content\"\n\n# Try to merge the cells\ncell1._element._move_content_to(cell2._element)\n\n# Save the document\ndoc.save(\"merged_cells.docx\")\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nAll content from the source cell should be properly moved to the target cell, and the source cell should be left with a single empty paragraph.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe content is not properly transferred between cells. When complex elements like structured document tags (SDT) or nested tables are involved, the content doesn't move correctly.\n\n## Additional context\n\nThis issue affects table cell merging operations when working with complex document structures. The problem seems to be in how the content elements are identified and moved between cells.\n</issue>\n",
